1
00:04:09,473 --> 00:04:15,473
When the law put up the money The Bounty Hunter put on his guns!

2
00:08:18,947 --> 00:08:24,947
The Bounty Hunter is a western, action film directed by André de Toth.

3
00:12:28,421 --> 00:12:34,421
A year after a violent train robbery the Pinkerton detective agency
hires a bounty hunter to find the three remaining killers.

4
00:16:37,894 --> 00:16:43,894
He tracks them to Twin Forks but has no clue to their identity.

5
00:20:47,368 --> 00:20:53,368
Tensions surface as just his presence in town acts as a catalyst.

6
00:24:56,842 --> 00:25:02,842
Jim Kipp / James Collins, played by Randolph Scott.

7
00:29:06,315 --> 00:29:12,315
Julie Spencer, played by Dolores Dorn.

8
00:33:15,789 --> 00:33:21,789
Alice Williams, played by Marie Windsor.

9
00:37:25,263 --> 00:37:31,263
Sheriff Brand, played by Howard Petrie.

10
00:41:34,736 --> 00:41:40,736
Dr. R.L. Spencer, played by Harry Antrim.

11
00:45:44,210 --> 00:45:50,210
George Williams, played by Robert Keys.

12
00:49:53,684 --> 00:49:59,684
The Bounty Hunter is a 1954 American western film directed by Andre DeToth
and starring Randolph Scott, Marie Windsor and Dolores Dorn.

13
00:54:03,157 --> 00:54:09,157
It was the last of six Randolph Scott westerns with DeToth and the
first film to feature a bounty hunter as its hero.

14
00:58:12,631 --> 00:58:18,631
It was released by Warner Bros.

15
01:02:22,105 --> 01:02:28,105
It was filmed in 3-D but released in standard format, though
a 3-D print exists in the Warner archives.

16
01:06:31,578 --> 01:06:37,578
Stock footage from the 1952 film Carson City is
used at the beginning of the film.

17
01:10:41,052 --> 01:10:47,052
Portions of the film were shot on location in California
at Red Rock Canyon and the Mojave Desert.

18
01:14:50,526 --> 01:14:56,526
The tone is dark.
